@startuml ConsoleReferenceArchitecture
' ============================================================================
' Reference architecture of a professional lighting console.
'
' Synthesised from the PUBLIC behaviour and documentation of grandMA3 and
' MagicQ (manuals, GDTF/MVR specs, protocol specs) - NOT from either vendor's
' source. Names follow MA3 where the two differ, with the MagicQ term in
' <<stereotype>> or in a note.
'
' Purpose: a target to compare LightEngine against. See the mapping notes at
' the bottom for what already exists in this project.
' ============================================================================

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam wrapWidth 260
hide empty members

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<def>>    #E3F2FD
  BorderColor<<def>>        #1565C0
  BackgroundColor<<patch>>  #FFF8E1
  BorderColor<<patch>>      #F9A825
  BackgroundColor<<show>>   #F3E5F5
  BorderColor<<show>>       #6A1B9A
  BackgroundColor<<prog>>   #E8F5E9
  BorderColor<<prog>>       #2E7D32
  BackgroundColor<<play>>   #FFEBEE
  BorderColor<<play>>       #C62828
  BackgroundColor<<out>>    #E0F7FA
  BorderColor<<out>>        #00838F
  BackgroundColor<<infra>>  #ECEFF1
  BorderColor<<infra>>      #455A64
}

legend top left
  <back:#E3F2FD> definition </back> <back:#FFF8E1> patch </back> <back:#F3E5F5> show data </back>
  <back:#E8F5E9> programmer </back> <back:#FFEBEE> playback </back> <back:#E0F7FA> output </back> <back:#ECEFF1> infrastructure </back>
endlegend

' ============================================================================
' 1. DEFINITION - what a fixture IS (GDTF)
' ============================================================================
package "1. Fixture Definition (GDTF / .hed)" as PDEF {

  class FixtureType <<def>> {
    name, shortName
    manufacturer
    fixtureTypeID : GUID
    revision
    thumbnail
  }

  class AttributeDefinitions <<def>> {
    activationGroups
    featureGroups
    attributes
  }

  class FeatureGroup <<def>> {
    name : Dimmer | Position | Gobo
    Color | Beam | Focus | Control
    Shapers | Video
    --
    the tabs on the encoder bar
  }

  class Feature <<def>> {
    name : PanTilt, RGB, Gobo1
    --
    one encoder page within a group
  }

  class Attribute <<def>> {
    name : Dimmer, Pan, Tilt,
      ColorAdd_R, Gobo1, Zoom, ...
    feature : Feature
    mainAttribute : Attribute
    physicalUnit
    colorSpace / color
    --
    ~400 standardised names
  }

  class ActivationGroup <<def>> {
    attributes that activate
    together (e.g. Pan+Tilt)
  }

  class Wheel <<def>> {
    name
    slots : WheelSlot
  }

  class WheelSlot <<def>> {
    name, color
    mediaFile (gobo image)
  }

  class PhysicalDescriptions <<def>> {
    emitters / filters
    colorSpace
    DMXProfiles
    CRIs
    properties (legHeight, weight)
  }

  class Emitter <<def>> {
    name
    spectrum
    dominantWaveLength
  }

  class Geometry <<def>> {
    name
    type : Axis | Beam | Normal
      MediaServerLayer | Display
    position : Matrix4
    children
  }

  class GeometryReference <<def>> {
    references a Geometry
    dmxOffset per break
    --
    THE mechanism for
    multi-cell / pixel fixtures
  }

  class DMXMode <<def>> {
    name : "Standard 16ch"
    footprint
    geometry : Geometry
    channels
    relations
  }

  class DMXChannel <<def>> {
    dmxBreak
    offset : coarse, fine, ultra
    initialFunction
    highlight
    geometry
  }

  class LogicalChannel <<def>> {
    attribute : Attribute
    snap : bool
    master : None|Grand|Group
    mibFade / dmxChangeTimeLimit
  }

  class ChannelFunction <<def>> {
    name
    attribute
    dmxFrom .. dmxTo
    physicalFrom .. physicalTo
    realFade / realAcceleration
    wheel / emitter / filter
    modeMaster (conditional)
  }

  class ChannelSet <<def>> {
    name : "Open", "Gobo 3"
    dmxFrom .. dmxTo
    physicalFrom .. physicalTo
    --
    the named slots a user picks
  }

  class DMXRelation <<def>> {
    master / follower channel
    type : Multiply | Override
  }

  class Macro_GDTF <<def>> {
    fixture-side macro
    (lamp on, reset, calibrate)
  }

  FixtureType *-- AttributeDefinitions
  FixtureType *-- PhysicalDescriptions
  FixtureType *-- Geometry
  FixtureType *-- DMXMode
  FixtureType *-- Wheel
  FixtureType *-- Macro_GDTF
  AttributeDefinitions *-- FeatureGroup
  AttributeDefinitions *-- ActivationGroup
  FeatureGroup *-- Feature
  Feature *-- Attribute
  Attribute --> ActivationGroup
  Wheel *-- WheelSlot
  PhysicalDescriptions *-- Emitter
  Geometry *-- GeometryReference
  DMXMode *-- DMXChannel
  DMXMode *-- DMXRelation
  DMXChannel *-- LogicalChannel
  LogicalChannel *-- ChannelFunction
  ChannelFunction *-- ChannelSet
  ChannelFunction --> WheelSlot
  ChannelFunction --> Emitter
  LogicalChannel --> Attribute
}

' ============================================================================
' 2. PATCH - what is in the rig
' ============================================================================
package "2. Patch / Rig" as PPATCH {

  class Patch <<patch>> {
    fixtures
    universes / breaks
    --
    patch() / unpatch()
    repatch() / renumber()
    checkOverlap()
    importMVR()
  }

  class Fixture <<patch>> {
    fixtureId : FID      (user-facing)
    cid : uint           (internal, unique)
    name
    fixtureType + dmxMode
    address : break + channel
    subfixtures / cells
    position : Matrix4 (from MVR)
    layer / class
    --
    MagicQ: "head"
  }

  class SubFixture <<patch>> {
    cell / pixel index
    own attribute set
    --
    from GeometryReference
    MA3: subfixture
    MagicQ: head cell
  }

  class DMXAddress <<patch>> {
    universe : uint16
    channel  : 1..512
    break    : uint
  }

  class Universe <<patch>> {
    number
    512 byte buffer
    priority (sACN)
    --
    one DMX512 frame
  }

  class DMXPort <<patch>> {
    protocol : sACN|ArtNet|MANet
      |sACN-in|DMX-XLR|Local
    universe mapping
    destination / interface
  }

  class MVRScene <<patch>> {
    3D positions
    layers
    fixture instances
    --
    interchange with CAD / viz
  }

  Patch *-- Fixture
  Fixture *-- SubFixture
  Fixture *-- DMXAddress
  Fixture --> FixtureType
  Fixture --> DMXMode
  Patch *-- Universe
  Universe --> DMXPort
  Patch <.. MVRScene
}

' ============================================================================
' 3. SHOW DATA - the numbered objects the user builds
' ============================================================================
package "3. Show Data (pools)" as PSHOW {

  class "Pool<T>" as PoolT <<show>> {
    numbered slots
    name index
    store / copy / move / delete
    labels, appearances
    --
    every object type is pooled
  }

  class DataPool <<show>> {
    MA3: a whole set of pools
    (groups, presets, sequences)
    swappable per user/show part
  }

  class Group <<show>> {
    ordered fixture selection
    --
    order matters: it drives
    effect/fan spatial index
  }

  class World <<show>> {
    attribute + fixture mask
    --
    "only Position of the spots"
    MagicQ: mask / filter
  }

  class Filter <<show>> {
    which attributes a store or
    playback is allowed to touch
  }

  class Preset <<show>> {
    featureGroup : Dimmer|Position
      |Gobo|Color|Beam|Focus|...
    mode : Universal | Global
      | Selective
    values per fixture (or generic)
    embedded phasers
    --
    MagicQ: palette
  }

  class Sequence <<show>> {
    cues (ordered, fractional nums)
    tracking on/off
    default timing
    off/release behaviour
    --
    MagicQ: cue stack
  }

  class Cue <<show>> {
    number : 1, 1.5, 2
    name
    parts
    trigger : Go|Follow|Time|Sound
      |Timecode
    fade / delay / in / out
    command (macro on cue)
  }

  class CuePart <<show>> {
    part number
    own fade/delay
    subset of values
  }

  class CueValue <<show>> {
    fixture + attribute -> value
    OR preset reference
    tracking state : Value|Tracked
      |Block|Assert|Release
    individual timing
    --
    reference beats value:
    edit the preset, cue follows
  }

  class Recipe <<show>> {
    MA3: group + preset + phaser
    resolved at runtime
    --
    a cue built from rules,
    not baked values
  }

  class Phaser <<show>> {
    MA3: the effect object
    steps with phase/width
    attribute layers
    grouping / wings
    --
    MagicQ: FX
  }

  class EffectTemplate <<show>> {
    reusable waveform + params
    (sine, saw, circle, fly-out)
  }

  class Macro <<show>> {
    ordered command lines
    wait / condition
  }

  class Layout <<show>> {
    2D arrangement of fixtures
    and pool objects
  }

  class View <<show>> {
    screen configuration
    (which windows, where)
  }

  class Page <<show>> {
    executor assignment set
    --
    MagicQ: playback page
  }

  class Timecode <<show>> {
    recorded events vs SMPTE/MIDI
    tracks -> executor commands
  }

  class Appearance <<show>> {
    colour + icon for pool objects
  }

  class UserProfile <<show>> {
    rights, keyboard, defaults
  }

  PoolT o-- Group
  PoolT o-- Preset
  PoolT o-- Sequence
  PoolT o-- World
  PoolT o-- Macro
  PoolT o-- Layout
  PoolT o-- Page
  PoolT o-- Phaser
  PoolT o-- Appearance
  DataPool *-- PoolT
  Sequence *-- Cue
  Cue *-- CuePart
  CuePart *-- CueValue
  Cue *-- Recipe
  CueValue ..> Preset : may reference
  Recipe --> Group
  Recipe --> Preset
  Recipe --> Phaser
  Preset ..> Phaser : may embed
  Phaser --> EffectTemplate
  Group --> Fixture
  World --> Attribute
}

' ============================================================================
' 4. PROGRAMMER - the live editing layer
' ============================================================================
package "4. Programmer" as PPROG {

  class Programmer <<prog>> {
    selection : ordered fixtures
    values (active / inactive)
    layers: Value|Timing|Phaser
    blind / preview mode
    highlight / lowlight / solo
    --
    clearAll() staged:
    values -> selection -> off
  }

  class Selection <<prog>> {
    ordered fixture list
    selection order drives fan
    subfixture selection
    --
    "next/prev/set/all"
  }

  class ProgrammerValue <<prog>> {
    fixture + attribute
    value (absolute or relative)
    state : Active | Inactive
    source : Manual|Preset|Effect
    preset reference (if any)
    individual fade/delay
  }

  class MAtricks <<prog>> {
    interleave / blocks / groups
    wings / shuffle / mirror
    x/y grid ordering
    --
    MagicQ: fan curves + groups
    reorders the spatial index
  }

  class Fan <<prog>> {
    spread a value across the
    selection: linear, symmetric,
    curved, from centre/ends
  }

  class EncoderBar <<prog>> {
    current FeatureGroup + Feature
    maps encoders to attributes
    --
    driven by AttributeDefinitions
  }

  Programmer *-- Selection
  Programmer *-- ProgrammerValue
  Programmer *-- MAtricks
  Programmer --> Fan
  Programmer --> EncoderBar
  Selection --> Fixture
  ProgrammerValue ..> Preset
  ProgrammerValue ..> Phaser
}

' ============================================================================
' 5. PLAYBACK - running the show
' ============================================================================
package "5. Playback / Execution" as PPLAY {

  class Executor <<play>> {
    fader + buttons
    assigned object (Sequence,
      Group, Preset, Macro...)
    priority
    fader function : Master|XFade
      |Rate|Speed|Temp
    off behaviour
    --
    MagicQ: playback
  }

  class CueEngine <<play>> {
    currentCue / nextCue
    go / goBack / goto / pause
    load / release / off
    assert / restart mode
    --
    the tracking state machine
  }

  class TrackingEngine <<play>> {
    computes each cue's OUTPUT
    from cue values + everything
    tracked in from earlier cues
    block / assert / release
    tracking-forward on edit
  }

  class Crossfade <<play>> {
    per-cue fade/delay
    in/out asymmetry
    per-attribute timing
    individual (per fixture) time
    fade curves
    snap attributes jump
  }

  class Chase <<play>> {
    sequence in chase mode
    rate / speed master
    direction, mode (bounce...)
  }

  class Master <<play>> {
    Grand Master
    group / feature masters
    speed masters (phaser rate)
    rate masters (cue time)
    highlight / solo
  }

  class PlaybackPriority <<play>> {
    per-executor priority
    HTP / LTP per attribute
    swap vs pile-on
    --
    decides who wins in the stack
  }

  Executor *-- CueEngine
  Executor --> PlaybackPriority
  CueEngine *-- TrackingEngine
  CueEngine *-- Crossfade
  CueEngine --> Sequence
  Executor --> Chase
  Executor --> Master
  Page o-- Executor
}

' ============================================================================
' 6. OUTPUT ENGINE - compositing to DMX
' ============================================================================
package "6. Output Engine" as POUT {

  class ValueStack <<out>> {
    per fixture + attribute:
    the ordered list of sources
    contributing this frame
    --
    default -> playbacks (by
    priority) -> programmer
  }

  class Compositor <<out>> {
    merges every source into
    one value per attribute
    HTP for dimmer,
    LTP for everything else
    applies masters
    --
    runs every output tick
  }

  class AttributeOwnership <<out>> {
    which source owns each
    attribute right now
    --
    required for release,
    solo and "what is active"
  }

  class ParkedValues <<out>> {
    fixture/channel forced to a
    value, bypassing the stack
  }

  class DMXRenderer <<out>> {
    physical -> DMX conversion
    channel functions + ranges
    coarse/fine/ultra split
    snap vs fade
    DMX profiles / curves
  }

  class UniverseBuffer <<out>> {
    512 bytes per universe
    double buffered
  }

  class OutputScheduler <<out>> {
    fixed-rate DMX thread
    (typically 25-44 Hz)
    decoupled from UI/render
    per-protocol timing
  }

  class ProtocolSender <<out>> {
    sACN / ArtNet / MA-Net
    Art-Net sync, sACN priority
    per-universe destinations
  }

  class DMXInput <<out>> {
    incoming DMX/sACN
    merge or trigger
  }

  ValueStack --> Compositor
  Compositor *-- AttributeOwnership
  Compositor --> ParkedValues
  Compositor --> DMXRenderer
  DMXRenderer --> UniverseBuffer
  UniverseBuffer --> OutputScheduler
  OutputScheduler --> ProtocolSender
  ProtocolSender --> DMXPort
  DMXRenderer ..> ChannelFunction : range lookup
  Programmer --> ValueStack
  Executor --> ValueStack
  Master --> Compositor
}

' ============================================================================
' 7. INFRASTRUCTURE
' ============================================================================
package "7. Infrastructure" as PINFRA {

  class CommandLine <<infra>> {
    keyword grammar:
    <verb> <object> <number>
    "Store Cue 3 Sequence 1"
    --
    EVERY UI action is a command
  }

  class CommandExecutor <<infra>> {
    resolves object references
    executes, returns result
    feeds undo stack
  }

  class UndoStack <<infra>> {
    MA3: Oops
    grouped transactions
    --
    only works if all mutation
    goes through commands
  }

  class ShowFile <<infra>> {
    serialise every pool object
    versioned, migratable
    autosave
    --
    needs generic object
    reflection to stay sane
  }

  class Session <<infra>> {
    multi-console networking
    master / tracking backup
    parameter sharing
    session state sync
  }

  class RemoteControl <<infra>> {
    OSC / MIDI / MIDI show control
    Timecode (LTC, MTC, ArtNet)
    DMX remote, GPIO
    web remote
  }

  class PluginHost <<infra>> {
    Lua (MA3) / scripting
    access to object model
  }

  class Visualizer <<infra>> {
    MA3D / Capture / WYSIWYG
    over MVR + DMX stream
  }

  class RealtimeCore <<infra>> {
    UI thread
    render/compositor thread
    DMX output thread(s)
    network thread
    --
    lock-free handoff of
    universe buffers
  }

  CommandLine --> CommandExecutor
  CommandExecutor --> UndoStack
  CommandExecutor ..> PSHOW
  CommandExecutor ..> PPROG
  CommandExecutor ..> PPLAY
  ShowFile ..> PSHOW
  ShowFile ..> PPATCH
  Session ..> RealtimeCore
  RemoteControl --> CommandExecutor
  PluginHost --> CommandExecutor
  Visualizer <.. ProtocolSender
  Visualizer <.. MVRScene
}

' ============================================================================
' Cross-package flow
' ============================================================================
PDEF -[hidden]-> PPATCH
PPATCH -[hidden]-> PSHOW
PSHOW -[hidden]-> PPROG
PPROG -[hidden]-> PPLAY
PPLAY -[hidden]-> POUT

note as NFLOW #FFFDE7
  **The output pipeline, every tick**
  1. Executors evaluate their current cue
     (tracking engine + crossfade + phasers)
  2. Programmer evaluates on top (highest priority)
  3. Compositor merges the ValueStack per attribute
     (HTP dimmer / LTP rest, masters applied)
  4. DMXRenderer converts physical -> DMX via
     ChannelFunction ranges, splits coarse/fine
  5. OutputScheduler ships universes on its own
     fixed-rate thread
end note
NFLOW .. POUT

note as NTRACK #FFEBEE
  **Tracking is the hard part**
  A cue stores only what CHANGED. The output of
  cue N is the accumulation of cues 1..N unless
  a Block or a new value interrupts it.
  Editing cue 3 must track forward through 4,5,6...
  Release/Off must revert only the attributes that
  source owned - hence AttributeOwnership.
end note
NTRACK .. TrackingEngine

note as NREF #E8F5E9
  **References, not copies**
  Cues store preset REFERENCES where possible.
  Change "Preset Color 5" and every cue using it
  updates. Same for groups inside recipes.
  This is why show data is a graph, not a tree,
  and why deletion needs reference counting.
end note
NREF .. CueValue

note as NMAP #ECEFF1
  **LightEngine today, mapped onto this**
  Have (some form of):
    GDTF: DMXChannel, LogicalChannel, Ranges, Attribute(6)
    Patch: Patch, UniversePatch, Fixture, FID/UID
    Show: Pool<T>, PoolObject, Group, Color preset
    Programmer: selection (Interval), static + animated effects
    Output: Frame + MergePolicy (= ValueStack + Compositor),
            ColorCell (= part of DMXRenderer), DMXOutput
  Missing entirely:
    FeatureGroup/Feature hierarchy, ChannelFunction/ChannelSet,
    GeometryReference (multi-cell), MVR,
    Sequence/Cue/CuePart/tracking, Executor/Page,
    World/Filter, MAtricks/Fan, Recipe,
    AttributeOwnership, ParkedValues,
    ShowFile, UndoStack, Session, Timecode,
    separate output thread
end note

@enduml
